IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `itaa-income`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1997, ss 4-10, 4-15, 6-5, 8-1, 26-55, 30-15, 36-10, 36-15, 36-17, 61-110, 61-115, 61-155, 61-160; Income Tax Rates Act 1986 s 3, Schedule 7 Part I, ss 23(2), 23AA -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_income-tax-assessment-act-1997_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`Chloe's course fee, connected to her current work (c083)` MEANS Outgoing WITH
    `incurred in gaining or producing assessable income` IS TRUE
    `necessarily incurred in carrying on a business` IS FALSE
    `capital or of a capital nature` IS FALSE
    `private or domestic` IS FALSE
    `relates to exempt or non-assessable non-exempt income` IS FALSE
    `another provision prevents the deduction` IS FALSE

`a course fee for a new career` MEANS Outgoing WITH
    `incurred in gaining or producing assessable income` IS FALSE
    `necessarily incurred in carrying on a business` IS FALSE
    `capital or of a capital nature` IS FALSE
    `private or domestic` IS FALSE
    `relates to exempt or non-assessable non-exempt income` IS FALSE
    `another provision prevents the deduction` IS FALSE

§ `s 4-15`

-- c045: Chloe's taxable income of $27,500.
#ASSERT `What is my taxable income` 27500 0 EQUALS 27500

§ `s 4-10 Step 2 and Rates Act Schedule 7`

-- c045: 2023-24 -- the deposited Rates Act has no resident table for that year, so NOTHING (not covered by the deposit).
-- c048: 2024-25, $71,500: (45,000 - 18,200) x 16% = 4,288 plus (71,500 - 45,000) x 30% = 7,950 = 12,238 (the scenario says 12,842).
-- k043: Jake, 2028-29, $31,000 as a sole trader: (31,000 - 18,200) x 14% = 1,792.
#ASSERT `What is my basic income tax liability` 2023 27500 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `What is my basic income tax liability` 2024 71500 EQUALS JUST 12238
#ASSERT `What is my basic income tax liability` 2028 31000 EQUALS JUST 1792

§ `ss 61-110, 61-115`

-- c045 ($27,500): $700. c048 ($71,500, above $66,667): nil. A foreign resident all year: nil.
#ASSERT `What Low Income tax offset do I get` TRUE 27500 EQUALS 700
#ASSERT `What Low Income tax offset do I get` TRUE 71500 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `What Low Income tax offset do I get` FALSE 27500 EQUALS 0

§ `ss 61-155, 61-160`

-- k043, IF Subdivision 61-E applies to 2028-29 (the application provision is not in the compilation): Jake's net labour
-- income of $31,000 exceeds $18,200; the notional liability is 1,792, so the offset is the cap of $250.
#ASSERT `What working Australians tax offset do I get` TRUE TRUE 2028 31000 EQUALS JUST 250

§ `s 4-10 Steps 3 and 4`

-- c048: 12,238 less no Low Income offset, Subdivision 61-E taken not to apply = 12,238.
-- k043: 1,792 - 700 = 1,092 without the working Australians offset; 1,792 - 700 - 250 = 842 with it.
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe` 2024 71500 FALSE 71500 EQUALS JUST 12238
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe` 2028 31000 FALSE 31000 EQUALS JUST 1092
#ASSERT `How much income tax do I owe` 2028 31000 TRUE 31000 EQUALS JUST 842

§ `s 6-5`

-- k043: Jake, a resident, on his sole-trader takings. A foreign resident's foreign-source income is not assessable.
#ASSERT `Is this ordinary income assessable to me` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Is this ordinary income assessable to me` FALSE FALSE

§ `s 8-1`

-- c083: Chloe's course at 40, connected to her current work, is deductible; a course for a new career is not.
#ASSERT `Can I deduct this outgoing` `Chloe's course fee, connected to her current work (c083)`
#ASSERT NOT `Can I deduct this outgoing` `a course fee for a new career`

§ `ss 36-10, 36-15, 36-17`

-- d04a: Jarrah's loss year (hypothetical figures): deductions 50,000 against income 30,000 give a loss of 20,000. Next year the
-- company may choose to deduct nil of it (s 36-17(2)); an individual with a 20,000 excess must deduct 20,000 of a 30,000 loss.
#ASSERT `What is my tax loss` 50000 30000 0 EQUALS 20000

#ASSERT `How much of its loss may my company deduct` 100000 40000 20000 0 EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `How much of my earlier loss must I deduct` 60000 40000 30000 EQUALS 20000

§ `ss 30-15, 26-55`

-- d072: Daniel's $2,000,000 to the Rossi Foundation, a private ancillary fund (item 2). d093: the gift in his will is not
-- deductible (s 30-15(2)). The s 26-55 limit on hypothetical income of 1,500,000 and other deductions of 100,000: 1,400,000.
#ASSERT `How much of my gift is deductible` 2000000 TRUE FALSE EQUALS 2000000
#ASSERT `How much of my gift is deductible` 2000000 TRUE TRUE EQUALS 0

#ASSERT `How much of my gift can I deduct this year` 2000000 TRUE FALSE 1500000 100000 EQUALS 1400000

§ `Rates Act ss 23(2), 23AA`

-- d04a: Jarrah, turnover $3,000,000 (hypothetical), no passive income: a base rate entity, 25%. A company whose income is 90%
-- passive is not: 30%.
#ASSERT `What rate does my company pay` 30000 0 3000000 EQUALS 25
#ASSERT `What rate does my company pay` 1000000 900000 3000000 EQUALS 30

